<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">
    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <!-- The saga's data and the port it is persisted through: what a case is opened with, what a
         confirmation lands as, what the sweeper hands back, the facts this service states about
         itself, and SagaStore.

         It DECLARES no compile-scope dependency, and the source honours that: every import under
         src/main is java.time or java.util, nothing else. But this is kept by hand, not by the
         build. The repository pom puts helidon-webserver, jackson-databind, kafka-clients,
         HikariCP, flyway, postgresql and logback-classic in a top-level <dependencies>, so every
         module inherits them — including this one. A type in here CAN import a broker, a database
         or a JSON library by mistake and still compile; it just has not. Said plainly because the
         comment that stood here until 2026-10-03 claimed the opposite guarantee and named those
         exact four things as impossible.

         Moving the repository's blanket dependencies into <dependencyManagement>, with each module
         declaring what it uses, is what would make the guarantee real — four modules' worth of
         declarations, and the owner's call, not a passing edit.

         The test-scoped line below is the saga's own vocabulary and nothing more: SagaStore's fake,
         which lives beside the port, is opened with a ClosureInitiator. -->
    <parent>
        <groupId>com.jrobertgardzinski</groupId>
        <artifactId>microservice-offboarding</artifactId>
        <version>1.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
    </parent>

    <artifactId>offboarding-domain</artifactId>
    <properties>
        <offboarding.repo.root>${project.parent.basedir}</offboarding.repo.root>
    </properties>

    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <!-- FakeSagaStore opens a case with the initiator the orchestrator was told about -->
            <groupId>com.jrobertgardzinski</groupId>
            <artifactId>account-closure</artifactId>
            <version>1.0.0-SNAPSHOT</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <plugin>
                <!-- SagaStore's fake and its contract travel to whoever implements or drives it -->
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-jar-plugin</artifactId>
                <executions>
                    <execution>
                        <goals>
                            <goal>test-jar</goal>
                        </goals>
                    </execution>
                </executions>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>
</project>
